 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to owner liability\nfor failure of an operator to comply with traffic-control devices in the\nvillage of Pelham Manor",
    "basePrintNo": "S9340",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9340-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1111-f, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9340\n\nSPONSOR: BIAGGI\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to owner\nliability for failure of an operator to comply with traffic-control\ndevices in the village of Pelham Manor\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo improve public safety.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends paragraph 1 of subdivision (a) of section 1111-f of\nthe vehicle and traffic law to provide that in the village of Pelham\nManor, where one of the two highways joining one another at such inter-\nsection is a state highway maintained by the state, such village may\ninstall and operate such traffic-control signal photo violation-monitor-\ning device in a manner affecting traffic proceeding along such state\nhighway at such intersection if it has obtained approval in writing from\nthe department of transportation, and the department of transportation\nmay at any time rescind or modify such approval.\n\nSection two provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapter 460 of the laws of 2021 authorized the village of Pelham Manor\nto install a red-light camera at no more than one intersection under the\njurisdiction of the village. As a result, the village installed a red-\nlight camera at the Pelhamdale Avenue/Boston Post Road intersection.\nHowever, only one of the roads at this intersection, Pelhamdale Avenue,\nis under the village's sole jurisdiction. Hence, the law does not allow\nfor the red-light cameras at this intersection to capture violations\noccurring on the Boston Post Road portion of the intersection, since\nBoston Post Road is a state-owned road.\n\nThis legislation will authorize Pelham Manor to install a red-light\ncamera to capture vehicles on Boston Post Road which fail to stop for a\nred light at this intersection, so long as the village first obtains\napproval in writing from the Department of Transportation. It is imper-\native that red light cameras cover the entirety of this intersection.\n\nThe village community has expressed concerns over the public's safety at\nthis intersection. There is a nursery school, shopping center and a\nnumber of elderly residents surrounding this intersection, as well as\nhigh school students who regularly use the crosswalks. Affording this\nauthorization to Pelham Manor will improve the safety of all who travel\nthrough or across the Pelhamdale Avenue/ Boston Post Road intersection.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law; provided, however, that the amendments to subdivision (a)\nof section 1111-f of the vehicle and traffic law made by section one of\nthis act shall not affect the repeal of such subdivision and shall be\ndeemed repealed therewith.\n",
